NEXHACKS STUDY - PROJECT CONTEXT
=================================

PROJECT NAME: PillPal (working title)

PROBLEM STATEMENT
-----------------
Medication non-adherence is a critical healthcare issue, especially among elderly populations. Studies show that 50% of patients do not take medications as prescribed, leading to 125,000 preventable deaths annually in the US alone. The elderly face unique challenges: cognitive decline, complex multi-drug regimens, vision/hearing impairments, and social isolation.

Current solutions (pill organizers, phone alarms) fail because they lack:
- Personalized guidance through complex medication schedules
- Verification that medication was actually taken
- Connection to caregivers/clinicians for oversight
- Holistic health tracking (diet, exercise) that affects medication efficacy

TARGET USERS
------------
Primary: Elderly patients (65+) with chronic conditions requiring multiple daily medications
Secondary: Clinicians, caregivers, and family members who monitor patient health

USER NEEDS (ELDERLY)
--------------------
- Simple, calm interface with large text and high contrast
- Voice-first interaction (reduces need for fine motor control)
- Gentle reminders that don't feel intrusive
- Clear visual confirmation of what to take and when
- Minimal cognitive load (one action at a time)
- Ability to track food and exercise with voice/photo input

USER NEEDS (CLINICIANS)
-----------------------
- Real-time adherence data across patient population
- Critical alerts for missed doses or concerning patterns
- Trend visualization for medication compliance
- Food/exercise logs to correlate with health outcomes
- Easy patient onboarding and medication schedule management

SOLUTION OVERVIEW
-----------------
Two-part system:

1. iOS Mobile App (Patient-Facing)
   - Minimal, calm design centered on a pill canister visual
   - Voice agent that walks patients through medication taking
   - Push notifications for medication reminders
   - Voice-guided food photography and exercise logging
   - Large touch targets, high contrast, readable fonts

2. Web Dashboard (Clinician-Facing)
   - Left sidebar navigation for different sections
   - Top navbar with search, notifications, profile
   - Patient list with adherence scores
   - Individual patient detail views with trends
   - Critical alerts panel for immediate attention
   - Food/exercise logs with timeline view

DATA ARCHITECTURE
-----------------
Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)

Core Tables:
- users (patients and clinicians)
- medications (drug info, dosage, frequency)
- medication_schedules (patient-specific schedules)
- medication_logs (actual taken events)
- food_logs (photos, voice transcriptions, timestamps)
- exercise_logs (type, duration, voice notes)
- alerts (missed doses, concerning patterns)

KEY FEATURES
------------
iOS App:
- Voice agent integration (likely OpenAI Realtime API or similar)
- Push notifications via APNs
- Camera integration for food photos
- Simple gesture-based interactions
- Offline-capable with sync

Web Dashboard:
- Real-time updates via Supabase subscriptions
- Data visualization (charts, trends)
- Patient management CRUD
- Alert management and acknowledgment
- Export capabilities for reports

DESIGN PRINCIPLES
-----------------
For Elderly Users:
- Minimum 16px base font, 18-20px preferred for body text
- High contrast ratios (WCAG AAA where possible)
- No reliance on color alone for information
- Large touch targets (minimum 44x44px)
- Consistent navigation patterns
- Voice as primary input method
- Visual feedback for all actions
- Calm color palette (avoid harsh colors)

For Clinician Dashboard:
- Information density balanced with clarity
- Quick actions accessible without deep navigation
- Clear data hierarchy
- Responsive for tablet use during rounds
- Keyboard shortcuts for power users

TECH STACK
----------
Frontend (Web): Next.js 16, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
Backend: FastAPI, Python 3.11+, Pydantic
Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + Realtime)
iOS App: React Native or Swift (TBD based on voice requirements)
Voice: OpenAI Realtime API or similar
Secrets: Infisical

