RESEARCH NOTES
--------------
Medication Adherence Statistics:
- 20-30% of prescriptions never filled
- 50% of medications not taken as prescribed
- Poor adherence causes 10% of hospitalizations
- $100-300 billion annual cost to US healthcare system

Elderly-Specific Challenges:
- 40% of adults 65+ take 5+ medications daily
- Cognitive decline affects medication management
- Vision impairment makes reading labels difficult
- Hearing loss impacts phone-based reminders
- Social isolation reduces accountability

Voice Interface Benefits for Elderly:
- Reduces need for reading small text
- Natural interaction pattern (like talking to a person)
- Can provide step-by-step guidance
- Confirms understanding through conversation
- Reduces anxiety around technology

Clinician Dashboard Best Practices:
- Prioritize actionable information
- Use progressive disclosure for details
- Support quick scanning of patient lists
- Highlight anomalies and urgent items
- Enable efficient batch operations

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (MVP)
-------------------------
iOS App:
- [ ] User can receive push notification reminder
- [ ] Voice agent can guide through taking one medication
- [ ] User can confirm medication was taken
- [ ] User can take photo of food with voice description
- [ ] Data syncs to Supabase

Web Dashboard:
- [ ] Clinician can log in
- [ ] Dashboard shows patient list with adherence scores
- [ ] Can view individual patient medication history
- [ ] Can see critical alerts
- [ ] Can view food/exercise logs

Backend:
- [ ] Auth via Supabase
- [ ] CRUD for patients, medications, schedules
- [ ] Logging endpoints for medications, food, exercise
- [ ] Alert generation logic
- [ ] Real-time subscriptions for dashboard

